{"type":"message","id":"b5eda113","parentId":"c0a3151a","timestamp":"2026-04-01T21:00:30.012Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I can see that Telegram is enabled and configured. The gateway shows it's running and connected. Now I need to prepare the update notification for Sam.\n\nSummary of findings:\n1. OpenClaw: Update available to version 2026.4.1 (via pnpm)\n2. Skills: All 1 checked skill is up to date. 77 skills cannot be checked automatically (no version hash available)\n3. Telegram channel: Enabled and configured, gateway is running\n\nNow I should send the notification to Sam about the OpenClaw update via Telegram. Since this is a cron job, I should send a message to the Telegram channel.\n\nHowever, the task says: \"If the task explicitly calls for messaging a specific external recipient, note who/where it should go instead of sending it yourself.\"\n\nLooking at the task description, it says \"notify Sam with the update details\" - Sam is the user. Since this is running on the Telegram channel, I should send a message there. Let me check what the default target would be. The task didn't specify a specific channel, so I should send it to where the user will receive it.\n\nActually, looking at the instruction more carefully: \"Return your summary as plain text; it will be delivered automatically.\" This suggests I should just return the summary and the delivery will be handled automatically. But then it also says: \"If the task explicitly calls for messaging a specific external recipient, note who/where it should go instead of sending it yourself.\"\n\nThe task says \"notify Sam with the update details\" - so I should notify Sam. Since this is a Telegram integration, I think I should send a message via the message tool. But let me re-read: \"Return your summary as plain text; it will be delivered automatically.\"\n\nI think the right approach is to:\n1. Prepare a summary in plain text format\n2. The cron job system will deliver it\n\nActually, looking at the delivery section of the cron job info, it mentions that for systemEvent jobs (which would deliver to a channel), there's a delivery.mode that can be \"announce|webhook\". \n\nThe default cron job uses an isolated session, which means the announcement should go to the channel where the job was created. I'll need to determine the correct channel for notifying Sam about the update details.\n\nThe message action seems straightforward: send a message to a target channel with the update information. I'll use the \"send\" action to pass along the OpenClaw update details directly to Sam's channel.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"🪶 **OpenClaw 및 스킬 업데이트 확인 결과**\n\n**OpenClaw 업데이트:**\n- 현재: 이전 버전\n- 최신: 2026.4.1 (npm) 사용 가능\n- 업데이트 명령: `openclaw update`\n\n**스킬 업데이트:**\n- 확인 가능한 스킬: 1개 (모두 최신 상태)\n- 자동 확인 불가: 77개 (버전 해시 없음)\n\n**Telegram 채널:**\n- 상태: 활성화 및 연결됨\n- Gateway: 정상 작동 중 (PID 259)\n\nSam에게 Telegram 메시지로 전송 필요합니다."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai","model":"glm-4.7","usage":{"input":5070,"output":1197,"cacheRead":25951,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":32218,"cost":{"input":0.003042,"output":0.0026334,"cacheRead":0.00285461,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.008530010000000001}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775077220213,"responseId":"2026040205002263740cf17eee4677"}}
